<%# The cheat sheet for the wall by the laser. Printing hides the rest of the page (print rules in pages/laser.scss); the paper size sets @page. %>
<% name, size = LaserController::PAPERS[@paper] %>
<style>@page { size: <%= size %>; margin: 0.4in; }</style>
<section class="card laser-printbar">
  <p>The settings on one sheet for the wall by the laser. Pick a paper size, then print with headers and footers off and background graphics on.</p>
  <nav class="filters" aria-label="Paper size">
    <% LaserController::PAPERS.each do |key, (label, _size)| %>
      <%= link_to label, laser_path(view: "sheet", paper: key), class: ["toggle", ("on" if key == @paper)], "aria-current": ("true" if key == @paper) %>
    <% end %>
    <button type="button" class="btn" data-controller="print" data-action="print#print">Print the <%= name %> sheet</button>
  </nav>
</section>

<article class="laser-sheet">
  <header>
    <h2>Large 80 W laser: settings that worked</h2>
    <p>Power % then speed mm/s: typical, the median of logged jobs that worked. Average is the mean of the same jobs. <span class="chip ok dot">90%+</span> <span class="chip warn dot">75 to 89%</span> <span class="chip err dot">under 75%</span> clean success. Grey rows: under 5 good jobs, or settings all over the place; a starting guess only.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="laser-sheet-body">
    <% @sheet[:cut].each do |family, rows| %>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th colspan="2">Cut: <%= family %></th><th class="num">Power</th><th class="num">Speed</th><th class="num">Pass</th><th class="num">Average</th><th class="num">Jobs</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <% rows.each_with_index do |row, i| %>
            <% s = row[:stats] %>
            <tr class="<%= "thin" if s[:basis] < 5 || s[:scattered] %>">
              <td><%= row[:material] if i.zero? || rows[i - 1][:material] != row[:material] %></td><td><%= row[:bucket] %></td>
              <td class="num big"><%= laser_number(s[:power]) %></td><td class="num big"><%= laser_number(s[:speed]) %></td><td class="num"><%= laser_number(s[:passes]) %></td>
              <td class="num"><%= laser_number(s[:power_mean], 1) %> / <%= laser_number(s[:speed_mean], 1) %></td>
              <td class="num"><span class="chip dot <%= s[:rate] >= 90 ? "ok" : s[:rate] >= 75 ? "warn" : "err" %>"><%= s[:n] %></span></td>
            </tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    <% end %>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Raster engrave, any thickness</th><th class="num">Power</th><th class="num">Speed</th><th class="num">Gap mm</th><th class="num">Average</th><th class="num">Jobs</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <% @sheet[:engrave].each do |row| %>
          <% s = row[:stats] %>
          <tr class="<%= "thin" if s[:basis] < 5 || s[:scattered] %>">
            <td><%= row[:material] %></td><td class="num big"><%= laser_number(s[:power]) %></td><td class="num big"><%= laser_number(s[:speed]) %></td>
            <td class="num"><%= s[:gap] ? laser_number(s[:gap], 2) : "" %></td><td class="num"><%= laser_number(s[:power_mean], 1) %> / <%= laser_number(s[:speed_mean]) %></td>
            <td class="num"><span class="chip dot <%= s[:rate] >= 90 ? "ok" : s[:rate] >= 75 ? "warn" : "err" %>"><%= s[:n] %></span></td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <% rates = @trouble.by_material %>
  <div class="laser-sheet-notes">
    <section><h3>Will not cut through?</h3>
      <p>Check focus and flatten the sheet: wrong focus height and warped stock both come up again and again in the log.</p>
      <p>Slow down before you add power or passes.</p>
      <p>Still weak, or one side of the bed cuts worse? The log points to a dirty lens or a bed out of level. Write it in Machine Notes. Optics work is for the laser maintainers only.</p></section>
    <section><h3>Known trouble</h3>
      <p>Plywood 9 mm and up: <%= rates[:thick_plywood].first %>% of cuts had trouble. Plan to finish with a saw or knife.</p>
      <p>MDF and hardboard change sheet to sheet: <%= rates[:mdf].first %>% of cuts had trouble. Test each new sheet.</p>
      <p>Paper, cardboard and foam core catch fire at slow speeds and sharp corners. Go fast and low. Black acrylic flares: space parts apart and watch for flame.</p>
      <p>LaserCut stuck at 87% or a soft dog error: restart LaserCut, then the laser, then the PC. Copy files off the USB stick first.</p></section>
    <section><h3>Every job</h3>
      <p>HeatSync laser certification is required before you use this machine. Never leave the laser while it is firing; keep the water spray in reach.</p>
      <p>Run a test cut on scrap: these numbers move with lens condition and stock. Clean the slats and tray when you finish.</p>
      <p>Log the job, failures included. This sheet is built from that log.</p></section>
  </div>
  <footer>Built from <%= number_with_delimiter(@jobs.count(&:settings?)) %> logged jobs with settings, <%= @jobs.first.date.year %> to <%= @jobs.last.date.year %>. Member reported, not guaranteed. HeatSync Labs, 108 W Main St, Mesa. Printed from members.heatsynclabs.org/laser, <%= Date.current.iso8601 %>.</footer>
</article>
